imgsensor: ov02b10: restore the capture and video mode timing structs

takePicture never delivered a JPEG. The stall reproduced as three 500 ms
ISP_WAIT_IRQ timeouts (PASS1_TG1_DON twice, then VS1) with IrqStatus(0), no
error interrupt anywhere, and the ISP registers configured correctly, which
is what made it look like an ISP or IMGO path problem. It is the sensor.

The reference driver this port came from ships with the .cap1,
.normal_video, .hs_video and .slim_video entries of imgsensor_info inside
one comment block, so all four read as zeros. capture() takes the cap1
branch whenever current_fps != 300, and AE lowers the preview frame rate
indoors, so on a real device that branch is always taken: pclk, line_length,
frame_length and min_frame_length all become 0.

The first AE exposure write then does this in write_shutter():

  shutter > imgsensor.min_frame_length - margin   [0u - 7: false, unsigned]
  -> imgsensor.frame_length stays 0
  reg 0x14/0x15 = frame_length - 0x4c4            [0 - 1220 = 0xfb3c]

64316 dummy lines on a 1220-line base is a 65536-line frame: at 27.15 us per
line the sensor emits one frame every 1.78 s. Measured VS1 interrupts during
the stall arrived exactly 1.78 s apart, which is what pinned this. Every
500 ms wait misses, the HAL gives up, and the preview restart reprograms the
mode registers, which is why preview always recovered.

Two changes:

- Uncomment the four mode structs. All five modes run the same
  1600x1200@30 register table, so they take the same values as .pre/.cap.
  This also fixes video recording, which reads the same zeroed structs.

- Floor imgsensor.frame_length at the mode base in write_shutter() and
  set_shutter_frame_length() before the dummy-line subtraction, so no
  future zeroed or undersized state can underflow it again.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
@@ -70,7 +70,14 @@
 		/*     following for GetDefaultFramerateByScenario()    */
 		.max_framerate = 300,
 	},
-	/*
+	/* All five modes run the same 1600x1200@30 register table. These
+	 * sub-mode structs were commented out in the reference driver; with
+	 * them zeroed, capture() and the video modes load pclk=0,
+	 * line_length=0, frame_length=0, and write_shutter()'s unsigned
+	 * (frame_length - 0x4c4) dummy-line computation underflows to 0xfb3c,
+	 * slowing the sensor to one frame every 1.78 s. Every pass-1 IRQ wait
+	 * then times out and takePicture never delivers a JPEG.
+	 */
 	.cap1 = {
 		.pclk = 16500000,            //record different mode's pclk
 		.linelength = 448,            //record different mode's linelength
@@ -114,7 +121,7 @@
 		.grabwindow_height = 1200,        //record different mode's height of grabwindow
 		.mipi_data_lp2hs_settle_dc = 85,//unit , ns
 		.max_framerate = 300,
-	},*/
+	},
 	.margin = 7,            //sensor framelength & shutter margin
 	.min_shutter = 4,        //min shutter
 	.max_frame_length = 0x7fff,//max framelength by sensor register's limitation
@@ -285,6 +292,15 @@
 		imgsensor_info.margin)) ? (imgsensor_info.max_frame_length -
 		imgsensor_info.margin) : shutter;
 
+	/* The dummy-line registers below hold (frame_length - 0x4c4),
+	 * unsigned. A frame_length under the 0x4c5 base - the zeroed state a
+	 * misconfigured mode switch leaves behind - underflows that to
+	 * ~0xfb3c dummy lines, one frame every 1.78 s, and every pass-1 IRQ
+	 * wait then times out. Floor it at the mode base.
+	 */
+	if (imgsensor.frame_length < imgsensor_info.pre.framelength)
+		imgsensor.frame_length = imgsensor_info.pre.framelength;
+
 	//frame_length and shutter should be an even number.
 	shutter = (shutter >> 1) << 1;
 	imgsensor.frame_length = (imgsensor.frame_length >> 1) << 1;
@@ -1863,6 +1879,15 @@
 		imgsensor_info.margin)) ? (imgsensor_info.max_frame_length -
 		imgsensor_info.margin) : shutter;
 
+	/* The dummy-line registers below hold (frame_length - 0x4c4),
+	 * unsigned. A frame_length under the 0x4c5 base - the zeroed state a
+	 * misconfigured mode switch leaves behind - underflows that to
+	 * ~0xfb3c dummy lines, one frame every 1.78 s, and every pass-1 IRQ
+	 * wait then times out. Floor it at the mode base.
+	 */
+	if (imgsensor.frame_length < imgsensor_info.pre.framelength)
+		imgsensor.frame_length = imgsensor_info.pre.framelength;
+
 	//frame_length and shutter should be an even number.
 	shutter = (shutter >> 1) << 1;
 	imgsensor.frame_length = (imgsensor.frame_length >> 1) << 1;
